{"version":"1","id":"69cb797a-c282-4c1b-aaee-352f254a77a2","handle":"freshcodeit","name":"Freshcode","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--I3mQ6_o7--/f_auto/v1721143240/squads/69cb797a-c282-4c1b-aaee-352f254a77a2","description":null,"is_squad":true,"x":-8.0397,"y":9.9297,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":13,"newest_post_at":"2025-02-18T09:06:15.856Z","oldest_post_at":"2024-08-11T11:21:14.509Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":1.0,"summary_length_avg":290.846154,"title_length_avg":67.307692,"title_length_var":720.059172,"tag_entropy":2.389661,"tag_diversity":1.384615,"top_tag_share":0.0,"avg_upvotes":2.461538,"median_upvotes":2.0,"avg_comments":0.153846,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.090909,"zero_engagement_share":0.0,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.476674,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"recency_skew":3.333333},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[0.6912,5.8971],"cadence_depth":[-9.3088,-9.25],"hype_variety":[-7.8676,-7.2206],"title_style":[-7.9118,-6.6324]},"top_tags":[["clojure",13],["webdev",3],["ai",2],["backend",2],["leadership",2],["open-source",1],["salesforce",1],["qa",1]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Once you try Clojure there is no way back","Clojure vs Common Lisp: Contrasting Approaches to Modern Development","Developer Happiness: Why Our Team Chooses Clojure"],"outlier":["Clojure in product. Would you do it again?, Ep. 8, \"ClojureScript is a Clojure killer app\", with Jereme Corrado, Mobot"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"wBhDCQKX6","title":"Open-source is like all eyes looking at it, with Cam Saul, Metabase","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/open-source-is-like-all-eyes-looking-at-it-with-cam-saul-metabase-wbhdcqkx6","summary":"Cam Saul, Founding Engineer & Chief Architect at Metabase, discusses the challenges and advantages of rewriting Metabase in Clojure, the benefits of hiring Clojure developers, and the trade-offs of using Clojure in a large codebase.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--NDEy0gk7--/f_auto/v1739869575/posts/wBhDCQKX6","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-18T09:06:15.856Z"},{"id":"5Am53d6Og","title":"You need boundaries to do a meaningful work, with Alexander Johannes, JustOn","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/you-need-boundaries-to-do-a-meaningful-work-with-alexander-johannes-juston-5am53d6og","summary":"Alexander Johannes, Head of Development at JustOn, discusses how Clojure became integral to their systems, attracting top talent and enabling the company to transform Salesforce's limitations into opportunities. He also shares insights on growing senior developers in-house and maintaining structure at scale while avoiding over-engineering.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--QC9g9JVD--/f_auto/v1739210445/posts/5Am53d6Og","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-10T18:00:45.757Z"},{"id":"UwPtoF0V3","title":"Clojure in product. Would you do it again?, Ep. 8, \"ClojureScript is a Clojure killer app\", with Jereme Corrado, Mobot","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/clojure-in-product-would-you-do-it-again-ep-8-clojurescript-is-a-clojure-killer-app-with-jer-uwptof0v3","summary":"Jereme Corrado, Mobot's former CTO, shares his experience building a robotics-powered QA platform using Clojure, which grew into a team of 15 developers. Key points include the importance of team attributes, AI integration while maintaining code quality, and using Clojure and ClojureScript across various parts of a project.","image":null,"num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-04T17:48:34.524Z"},{"id":"GKwyz04gd","title":"And until you get to that point, you should be living in pain, right? - Episode 7, with Nathan Marz, Red Planet Labs","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/and-until-you-get-to-that-point-you-should-be-living-in-pain-right---episode-7-with-nathan-marz--gkwyz04gd","summary":"In Episode 7 of 'Clojure in Product: Would You Do It Again?', Nathan Marz discusses building a Twitter-scale app using the Rama platform, which drastically reduces backend complexity. The conversation also covers forming scalable teams around Clojure and a revolutionary event sourcing architecture.","image":null,"num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-27T19:55:04.494Z"},{"id":"Yzz7S0zss","title":"Episode 6: \"I truly discovered the enlightenment with Clojure\"","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/episode-6-i-truly-discovered-the-enlightenment-with-clojure--yzz7s0zss","summary":"Yehonathan Sharvit, Infrastructure Architect at CyCognito, shares his journey from struggling with C++ to discovering the benefits of Clojure in enterprise cybersecurity. The episode also discusses an unexpected success arising from a failed book project and the substantial influence of Clojure.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--wp89Jo94--/f_auto/v1737478952/posts/Yzz7S0zss","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-21T17:02:32.061Z"},{"id":"1TbBtQLWk","title":"\"Clojure in product. Would you do it again?\" 5th episode","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/clojure-in-product-would-you-do-it-again-5th-episode-1tbbtqlwk","summary":"A tech lead shares his journey from PHP to Clojure during the lockdown, exploring rebuilding an API stack for a travel platform serving multiple European countries. The episode highlights the choice of Clojure for travel platform APIs, learning alongside a team, and the supportive Clojure community. It also addresses managing the state in a growing system.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--rCic8OCe--/f_auto/v1736797087/posts/1TbBtQLWk","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-13T19:38:06.815Z"},{"id":"Ehj9ZXlkH","title":"Is it easy to manage a team of highly qualified engineers? Clojure in Product podcast, episode 4","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/is-it-easy-to-manage-a-team-of-highly-qualified-engineers-clojure-in-product-podcast-episode-4-ehj9zxlkh","summary":"Griffin's VP of Engineering, James Trunk, discusses the unique approach to building a banking technology platform using Clojure. Learn about their method of embracing immutable data and a flexible 'molding clay' approach to coding in a regulated environment.","image":null,"num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-06T10:54:29.215Z"},{"id":"umvSnxpAM","title":"Once you try Clojure there is no way back","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/once-you-try-clojure-there-is-no-way-back-umvsnxpam","summary":"Discover how Marten Sytema's use of Clojure in the Catermonkey project turned a custom solution into a scalable platform. The episode explores guerilla tactics in technology adoption, the unique dynamics of smaller talent pools, and the irreversible impact of certain technical decisions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--Meslle1G--/f_auto/v1734459876/posts/umvSnxpAM","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-17T18:24:36.437Z"},{"id":"aQioTGMNh","title":"Clojure in Product. Would you do it again? 2nd episode","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/clojure-in-product-would-you-do-it-again-2nd-episode-aqiotgmnh","summary":"Join programming expert Adam Tornhill in the latest podcast episode as he delves into the art of behavioral code analysis, tackles technical debt, and discusses the reasons behind CodeScene's choice of Clojure. Plus, gain insights on AI and its integration with Clojure from our previous discussion.","image":null,"num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-09T21:00:05.506Z"},{"id":"NG8qLxFEE","title":"Clojure in Product podcast","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/clojure-in-product-podcast-ng8qlxfee","summary":"New podcast 'Clojure in Product' features real stories of teams using Clojure in production. The first episode discusses the experience of integrating Clojure into a Java-based enterprise system with guest Kalle Korhonen from Quuppa.","image":null,"num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-03T17:26:10.198Z"}],"similar_handles":["fluttersquad","dailyopensourcetools","dev_world","404","sknexus"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","xai","hwchase17","hamelhusain","skirano"],"similar":[{"id":"fbd063d4-1b63-434f-89c3-a74e585e4ba8","handle":"fluttersquad","name":"Flutter Developers","is_squad":true,"x":-8.0414,"y":9.8686,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":16,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--fgc43Pla--/f_auto/v1745371182/squads/fbd063d4-1b63-434f-89c3-a74e585e4ba8","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.182529,"median_upvotes":1.5,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.03125,"avg_read_time":1.625,"tag_diversity":1.5625},"top_tags_preview":[["flutter",14],["mobile",8],["dart",7]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[2.1324,9.8824],"cadence_depth":[-8.8235,-8.25],"hype_variety":[6.7941,-4.3676],"title_style":[9.6765,-6.7206]}},{"id":"efbb7001-f465-4dca-a829-5e56b672f8b2","handle":"dailyopensourcetools","name":"Daily Open Source Tools","is_squad":true,"x":-8.2193,"y":10.0518,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":33,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ljDCWNBZ--/f_auto/v1731669074/squads/efbb7001-f465-4dca-a829-5e56b672f8b2","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.480825,"median_upvotes":4.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":1.69697,"tag_diversity":2.424242},"top_tags_preview":[["open-source",12],["devtools",7],["webdev",4]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[7.0294,6.0147],"cadence_depth":[-6.3824,-8.1029],"hype_variety":[-8.6912,7.8676],"title_style":[3.2794,-7.8824]}},{"id":"81a3df5b-e17a-41f0-ae4f-8035927c6518","handle":"dev_world","name":"Dev World","is_squad":true,"x":-8.3798,"y":9.9969,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":29,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--qM3M5FZK--/